<title>UK: Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs rise in week.</title>
<headline>Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs rise in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of active oil and gas rigs in operation offshore northwest Europe rose by two to 57 in the week to September 18, consultants Arthur Andersen said.</p>
<p>The U.K. sector rose by two to 31 acive rigs while the Norwegian sector fell by one to 13 rigs.</p>
<p>Danish activity was steady on the week at four rigs while the Dutch sector rose one to eight rigs. Irish activity was unchanged at one.</p>
<p>Onshore drilling activity was unchanged at three rigs, two in the U.K. and one in the Faroe Islands.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 6280</p>
